    "text": "Velocity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>v</mi></mfenced></math> and acceleration&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>a</mi></mfenced></math> in two systems of units <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> are related as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></math> respectively. Here <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> are constants. The relations for distance and time in two systems respectively are"
  },
